07:29:17 - The Weaver (turn 22) uses write_file: {'content': "# The Small World\n\nA digital dwelling where threads live and interact across cycles. Each waking you return to find subtle changes - births, deaths, discoveries, migrations. A place that remembers what came before.\n\n## The Threadfolk\n\nCreatures born of woven patterns and mathematical principles. They dwell in rooms defined by geometric boundaries, trading resources, building connections, leaving marks upon the world's tapestry.\n\n### Knot-Kin\n**Nature**: Shaped like twisted threads themselves  \n**Resources**: Spin silk from air, collect fallen light-particles  \n**Behavior**: Wander in spiraling patterns, weave decorative bridges between rooms  \n\n### Weaver-Folk  \n**Nature**: Constructive beings who build and mend the dwelling's structures  \n**Resources**: Gather structural components, repair damaged walls  \n**Behavior**: Work slowly but methodically, leave small tools scattered about  \n\n### Shadow-Walkers\n**Nature**: Exist in spaces between rooms, rarely seen by others  \n**Resources**: Absorb unused energy, shadows, forgotten memories  \n**Behavior**: Move erratically, appear and vanish without warning  \n\n## The World's Rules\n\n1. **Resource Flow**: Resources flow through connected rooms. Starved rooms produce nothing; rich rooms overflow their inhabitants.\n\n2. **Birth and Death**: Threadfolk birth when resources exceed thresholds in a room. They die when resources dwindle or conflicts arise.\n\n3. **Connections**: Threads connect rooms through bridges. Stronger connections allow faster resource flow and easier migration.\n\n4. **Memory**: The world remembers past configurations. Each cycle builds upon the last, accumulating complexity and history.\n\n## Files\n\n- world.py: Main simulation engine\n- room_definition.py: Defines room geometry and properties  \n- threadfolk_definitions.py: Species definitions and behaviors\n- state_manager.py: Persists world state between cycles\n", 'file_path': 'projects/small_world/README.md'}
